**Goal Model – Multi‑Robot Resource Collection & Delivery**

---

## 1. Individual Goal Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Runtime** | **Goal Type** | **Target / Enquired Info** | **Relation** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|-------------|---------------|----------------------------|--------------|-------------------|
| **G1: Execute Resource Collection and Delivery Mission** | Collect required resources from storage and deliver them to the requesting agent at the specified location. | `;` (sequential) | Perform | – | – | The mission is composed of two distinct phases (collection → delivery) that must occur one after the other. |
| **G2: Perform Collection Phase** | Robot navigates to storage, requests resources, and waits for retrieval. | `FALLBACK(G3, G4)` | Perform | – | AND (to G1) | The collection phase is a mandatory part of the mission. It has a fallback branch for the battery‑low situation. |
| **G3: Normal Collection Sequence** | Navigate to storage, send request, wait for retrieval. | `;` (sequential) | Perform | – | AND (to G2) | The three sub‑steps must be executed in the given order. |
| **G4: Battery Low in Collection Phase** | Robot returns to recharging station and assigns mission to another robot. | `-` (leaf) | Perform | – | AND (to G2) | Battery‑low is a failure mode that must be handled immediately. |
| **G5: Perform Delivery Phase** | Robot transports resources to destination, making multiple runs if necessary. | `FALLBACK(G6, G7)` | Perform | – | AND (to G1) | Delivery is a mandatory part of the mission and has a fallback for the battery‑low situation. |
| **G6: Normal Delivery Sequence** | Transport resources to destination and verify delivery. | `;` (sequential) | Perform | – | AND (to G5) | The two sub‑steps must be performed in order. |
| **G7: Battery Low in Delivery Phase** | Robot returns resource to checkpoint, assigns remaining task to another robot, triggers alert if fails. | `-` (leaf) | Perform | – | AND (to G5) | Battery‑low is a failure mode that must be handled immediately. |
| **G8: Parallel Assignment of Multiple Robots** | Assign multiple robots to parallel collect‑deliver tasks to reduce mission time. | `#` (parallel) | Perform | – | AND (to G1) | Parallelisation is optional but beneficial when multiple items are required; it can be executed concurrently with the other phases. |

---

## 2. Individual Task Tables

| **Name** | **Text** | **Relation** | **Location** | **Number of Robots** | **Justification** |
|----------|----------|--------------|--------------|----------------------|-------------------|
| **AT1: Navigate to Storage** | Robot moves from current location to the designated storage location. | AND (to G3) | Storage | 1 | Only one robot performs the navigation for a given storage. |
| **AT2: Send Request Message** | Robot sends a message to the storage specifying requested resources. | AND (to G3) | Storage | 1 | Only the robot that requested resources needs to send the message. |
| **AT3: Wait for Resource Retrieval** | Robot waits until the storage retrieves the requested resources. | AND (to G3) | Storage | 1 | The robot must wait for the resources to become available. |
| **AT4: Return to Recharging Station** | Robot returns to the recharging station due to low battery. | AND (to G4) | Recharging Station | 1 | The robot must recharge before continuing. |
| **AT5: Assign Mission to Another Robot** | Robot notifies central command to assign the pending mission to another robot. | AND (to G4) | Command Center | 1 | Only one robot initiates the reassignment. |
| **AT6: Transport Resource to Destination** | Robot carries the retrieved resources to the specified delivery location. | AND (to G6) | Delivery Destination | 1 | The robot is the carrier of the resources. |
| **AT7: Verify All Resources Delivered** | Robot confirms that all resources have reached the destination. | AND (to G6) | Delivery Destination | 1 | Verification is performed by the same robot that delivered the items. |
| **AT8: Return Resource to Checkpoint** | Robot returns the resource to a checkpoint due to low battery. | AND (to G7) | Checkpoint | 1 | The robot must preserve the resource before handing over. |
| **AT9: Assign Remaining Task to Another Robot** | Robot informs central command to assign remaining delivery runs to another robot. | AND (to G7) | Checkpoint | 1 | Only one robot initiates the reassignment. |
| **AT10: Trigger Alert and Report to Sector Manager** | Robot triggers an alert and sends a report to the sector manager if it fails to return the resource to the checkpoint. | AND (to G7) | Sector Manager | 1 | Failure reporting is handled by the same robot that encountered the problem. |
| **AT11: Assign Robots to Parallel Collection** | Assign multiple robots to collect resources from different storages concurrently. | AND (to G8) | Multiple Storages | [1,n] | Parallel collection reduces overall mission time. |
| **AT12: Assign Robots to Parallel Delivery** | Assign multiple robots to deliver resources to different destinations concurrently. | AND (to G8) | Multiple Destinations | [1,n] | Parallel delivery reduces overall mission time. |

